                "Selecting the statutory benchmark: Aegis is a publicly listed commercial enterprise whose primary equity investors and debt rating agencies evaluate financial health through normalized operating profitability. Your engagement team analyzes four competing benchmark candidates: Normalized Profit Before Tax ($480M at 5% = $24.0M); Consolidated Gross Revenue ($9.8B at 0.5% = $49.0M); Total Assets ($14.2B at 0.5% = $71.0M); and Shareholder Equity ($5.2B at 1% = $52.0M). Because Aegis is a profit-oriented public interest entity, Normalized Profit Before Tax represents the primary metric driving investor valuation models. Applying the standard 5.0% multiplier for listed public entities yields an Overall Financial Statement Materiality (Planning Materiality) of exactly $24,000,000.",
